==Acquisition==
Incarnon Weapons can be acquired by:
*Completing [[Angels of the Zariman]], and then purchasing the weapon blueprints with [[The Holdfasts]] standing from [[Cavalero]] in [[Chrysalith]]. Additionally, these blueprints require the player to be at least [[Mastery Rank|Mastery Rank 14]], and are [[Trading|tradeable]].
*Completing [[Whispers in the Walls]] and [[The Deadlock Protocol]], and then running [[Armatus]], [[Deimos]] for a chance of the weapon blueprint and parts as part of a [[Rotation]] reward. Alternatively, collecting enough {{Resource|Vessel Capillaries}} from Armatus will allow the player to buy the blueprints and parts from [[Loid (Original)|Loid]] in [[Sanctum Anatomica]].
*Completing [[The Hex (Quest)|The Hex]], and then running [[Isleweaver]] on [[Duviri]] to collect enough {{Resource|Scuttler Husk}} to purchase the {{Weapon|Thalys}} weapon blueprint from [[Acrithis]] or [[Dominus Thrax]] in the [[Dormizone]].

Incarnon Geneses can be acquired by:
*Completing [[The Duviri Paradox]] and unlocking [[The Steel Path]], and then running [[The Circuit]] with the Steel Path modifier enabled to obtain up to two [[Incarnon Genesis|Incarnon Genes]]es every week. The rotation of Incarnon Geneses available changes with each week and can be seen in the table below. Genesis items can be installed on weapons by talking to [[Cavalero]] with the [[Duviri]] [[resources]] required.
*Alternatively, the player may purchase the current week's available Genesis Adapters '''once''' from Cavalero's "Incarnon market" for {{pc|120}}. This purchase also provides the resources used to install it.

Cavalero can also remove the Incarnon upgrade to return the Genesis Adapter, but the Duviri resources used for the installation are '''not''' refunded.

====Reward Rotation====
