==Mechanics==
[[File:IncarnonWeaponIndicator.png|thumb|x150px|right|UI indicator for Incarnon Transmutation]]
By completing a number of challenges based on the weapon, Incarnon weapons can be evolved. Like other challenges (Riven mods, Nightwave, etc.), progress is tracked independently from mission progress. Each weapon has a total of '''4 or''' '''5''' evolutions.

The first evolution unlocks the weapon's Incarnon Form, granting them an [[Alternate Fire]] mode or increasing their stats, while also changing their appearances. Activating the Incarnon Form requires certain conditions be met in missions, the method of which differs depending on the weapon.

For primary and secondary weapons (e.g. {{Weapon|Laetum}}, {{Weapon|Phenmor}}, {{Weapon|Felarx}}), the Incarnon Transmutation gauge that appears under the reticle must be charged by landing [[Enemy Body Parts|weakpoint hits]]. {{Resource|Angstrum Incarnon Genesis}} and {{Resource|Torid Incarnon Genesis}} are instead charged through direct hits. While active, the Incarnon Form uses its own separate ammunition, represented by the Transmutation gauge. Activating the Incarnon Form can be done at any level of charge, but the amount of Incarnon ammunition available will depend on how full the gauge was at the time the weapon transformed. Manually deactivating Incarnon Form by hitting Alt Fire again will deplete the entire gauge. When Incarnon Form ends, the weapon's magazine will be refilled with ammunition that is newly generated, rather than pulled from the weapon's reserve.

For melees (e.g. {{Weapon|Praedos}}, {{Weapon|Innodem}}), the Incarnon Form is activated by reaching a 6x [[Melee Combo]] (5x for Innodem) and then executing a [[Heavy Attack]]. Melee Incarnon Forms last for 180 seconds (90 seconds for Innodem and {{Weapon|Ruvox}}) and cannot be refreshed or canceled while active. This does not require consuming Melee Combo, so options such as [[Tennokai]] can be used to maintain the multiplier into Incarnon Form. 

The remaining Evolutions provide '''2 or 3''' different selectable perks that further enhance the weapon's stats. Only one perk can be selected per Evolution, which can be changed freely with Cavalero or in the [[Arsenal]].

===Challenges===
Below are the challenges required to unlock the Evolutions of each natural Incarnon weapon currently available (Incarnon Genesis challenges appear in the next section). The first, fourth, and fifth challenges are identical between these Incarnon weapons, but the second and third Evolutions differ between weapons.

Progress for all challenges is maintained between runs, so the player does not have to complete them in a single mission.

*Evolution I: Kill 100 enemies with the weapon
*Evolution II:
**Laetum/Phenmor/Felarx/Onos/Ruvox: Kill 8 [[Eximus]] with the weapon's Incarnon Form
**Praedos/Innodem: Activate Incarnon Form 6 times in a mission
*Evolution III:
**Laetum/Phenmor/Felarx: Land 8/20/20 weakpoint hits on [[Void Angel]]s with Primary fire without reloading
**Praedos/Innodem: Complete 3 Heavy Attacks on [[Thrax Centurion]]s or [[Thrax Legatus|Legates]]
**Onos: Get '''5''' weakpoint hits on [[Scathing Whisper|Scathing]] and [[Mocking Whisper]]s in Albrecht's Laboratories with Primary fire without reloading.
**Ruvox: Inflict 3 Heavy Attacks on Scathing and Mocking Whispers in Albrecht's Laboratories
*Evolution IV:
**Zariman Ten Zero: Close 12 Ruptures in [[Void Flood]]
***Player ''must'' have contributed to closing the rupture via depositing Vitoplast.
**Albrecht's Laboratories: Open 20 Conduits in [[Disruption]] on [[Armatus]], [[Deimos]].
*Evolution V: Complete a Solo mission with an Incarnon Weapon equipped in every slot
**''Any'' mission will suffice for this challenge.
**Incarnon Genesis weapons are valid for the purposes of this challenge.

===Incarnon Genesis===
{{Quote|<big>Incarnon Genesis</big>

Hey.

Heard you been grubbing around in the [[Zariman]]'s backyard. That little tinpot '[[Duviri|kingdom]].'

Well, in my extensive downtime, I've been having thoughts about weapons. How I could upgrade 'em. Give 'em a sprinkle of Void magic. And guess what? The Void does what the Void does. [[Conceptual Embodiment|Took my ideas and made them real.]] How about that.

So if you've picked up a... let's call it an Incarnon Genesis, why not? An Incarnon Genesis, bring it to me and I'll get it installed for ya.

Slaughter awaits.<br/>
[[Cavalero]]

PS. [[Yonta]] says I need to say this very clearly: I cannot adapt a weapon you do not own. I will need both the Incarnon Genesis AND the weapon it applies to. Understood? I am not running a charity here.}}

Similarly to the Zariman weapons, the Genesis weapons have their own challenges, but only have '''4''' Evolutions in total. Installing the Genesis Adapter is considered the first challenge. Challenges only need to be cleared once per weapon type. For example, clearing {{Weapon|Braton}}'s challenges will automatically unlock perks for {{Weapon|Mk1-Braton}}, {{Weapon|Braton Prime}}, and {{Weapon|Braton Vandal}} when acquiring their Incarnon forms. The remaining challenges are as follows:

*Evolution II: Complete a solo mission with the weapon
*Evolution III:
**Primary/Secondary: Kill 100 enemies with the weapon's Incarnon Form
**Melee: Activate Incarnon Form 6 times in a mission
*Evolution IV: Varies by weapon

